   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = \\frac{\\left(x^{2} + 2 x - 3\\right)\\left(x^{2} - 7 x + 10\\right)}{\\left(x^{2} - 6 x + 5\\right)\\left(x^{2} - 9\\right)} \\). The graph of \\( f \\) has exactly one vertical asymptote, the line \\( x = c \\). Find the value of \\( c \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator factors as \\( \\left(x - 5\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) \\left(x - 1\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) \\) and the denominator as \\( \\left(x - 5\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) \\left(x - 1\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               5
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               1
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The factors at \\( x = -3 \\), \\( x = 1 \\), and \\( x = 5 \\) divide out, so \\( f(x) = \\frac{x - 2}{x - 3} \\) for \\( x \\neq -3, 1, 5 \\). Those three inputs are removable discontinuities, not asymptotes.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "After cancelling, the denominator is zero only at \\( x = 3 \\), and the numerator is not zero there.",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The one sided limits are \\( \\lim_{x \\to 3^-} f(x) = -\\infty \\) and \\( \\lim_{x \\to 3^+} f(x) = \\infty \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "So the line \\( x = 3 \\) is the only vertical asymptote, and \\( c = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
